[2026-11-15T10:25:20.292Z] entry text MISSIONFORGE A TEAM MISSION-DESIGN GAME Build a spacecraft with your team: choose the parts, balance mass, power, budget, instruments, orbit and communications, then vote and launch together. One big screen shows the mission; everyone plays on their phone. Unofficial educational game. Not affiliated with or endorsed by NASA. BIG SCREEN Host a mission Open this on the shared screen or projector. It creates a room and shows the room code and a QR code. Best on a laptop or desktop browser. Full screen, 1920×1080. Host a mission (big screen) PHONE Join on your phone Enter the room code from the big screen, or scan its QR code. Vote on parts, run your console, play the minigames. No account, no install, no chat. Join on your phone AUDIENCE Watch as audience Follow the mission and cast audience votes without a seat on the crew. Add the room code on the next screen. Watch as audience HOW A SESSION RUNS One screen hosts; up to ten players join with a room code. The crew votes on each part: its mass, power, cost and risk are shown for every option. Launch, fly and fix problems together; each role has its own console. See the score and debrief what the physics and the budget taught you. How to play (full guide) Credits, data sources and licences For judges (JUDGES.md) Offline demo (no server) MissionForge uses generic hardware names. Numbers are tagged physical, real-world approximate or game value.
